  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1407
    notes: The NBRC1407 footnote defines the process for its25% yeast extract solution.
      This is not a product-equivalence claim to commercial dry extract or whole yeast
      biomass.
notes: 'Preparation: suspend250g dried baker''s yeast in1L distilled water, boil30minutes,
  remove yeast cells by centrifugation and sterilize the resulting liquid by filtration.
  The recipe calls this25%Yeast extract solution and adds100ml to PPLO broth. The25%
  wording describes starting biomass loading; recovered supernatant volume, soluble
  yield, organism strain and analyte composition are not measured. Nohas-part assertion
  of250g retained cells or250g/L final dissolved extract is made. Raw source label:
  ''25% Yeast extract solution'''
